---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t, type Locale } from '../i18n/ui';
import { localizedPath } from '../i18n/utils';

interface Props { locale: Locale; }
const { locale } = Astro.props;
---

<BaseLayout locale={locale} title={t(locale, 'about.title')}>
  <article class="container about-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>{t(locale, 'about.title')}</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="article-content">
      {locale === 'ko' ? (
        <>
          <p>
            제 <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'resume/')}>레쥬메</a>와 <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'cv/')}>CV</a>도 함께 올려두었습니다.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>I am a student majoring in computer science. I live with a constant curiosity about “why?” in everything.</p>
          <p>
            I learned programming because I was curious about how the programs I see on screen are made.
            As I learned programming, I became curious about how programs actually work, so I studied computer systems.
            I then became curious about how source code, which is ultimately just text, is translated into machine code,
            and that led me to study compilers. Through that process, I naturally developed an interest in compilers and information security.
          </p>
          <p>
            These days, I try to spend a little less time looking at monitors and experience the world with my whole body.
            Even though I kept printing <code>hello, world</code> on the screen, I realized that I may have been rather indifferent to the world itself.
          </p>
          <p>
            Here, I plan to record the things I learn while studying computer science, as well as the thoughts I gather while living through the world.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can also find my <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'resume/')}>résumé</a> and <a href={localizedPath(locale, 'cv/')}>CV</a> here.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <hr />

